WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.329
Scenario: You receive an SMS claiming a parcel is

2
00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:06.658
held for a small delivery fee. It includes a

3
00:00:06.658 --> 00:00:10.356
shortened link and says the parcel will be returned today.

4
00:00:10.356 --> 00:00:13.685
Safest response: Option D: Use the courier’s official app

5
00:00:13.685 --> 00:00:17.014
or independently located website to check tracking; do not

6
00:00:17.014 --> 00:00:20.342
use the SMS link. Verify parcel status independently rather

7
00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:23.671
than following an unsolicited link. Option A is unsafe

8
00:00:23.671 --> 00:00:27.740
because Providing personal information to an unverified sender creates additional exposure.

9
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.068
Option B is unsafe because A small payment request

10
00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:34.767
